WEBVTT

00:00:08.750 --> 00:00:11.208
Having obtained certain information,

00:00:11.208 --> 00:00:14.000
we were now secretly investigating the truth.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:15.750
Or so our cover story went.

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:18.958
In fact, we'd infiltrated this café
a good ways from school

00:00:18.958 --> 00:00:21.000
just for the heck of it.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:23.583
Wow, what a man!

00:00:25.167 --> 00:00:28.542
Welcome! Ah, always good to see you,

00:00:28.542 --> 00:00:30.208
Mrs. Harada and Mrs. Ito.

00:00:30.208 --> 00:00:32.708
How's it going, little Yuma?

00:00:32.708 --> 00:00:36.083
We come here more for
you than for the coffee!

00:00:36.083 --> 00:00:40.250
Now don't say that. Wouldn't want
the owner to head to the dark side.

00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:44.208
So, a mocha for you, Mrs. Harada,
and a double espresso for Mrs. Ito?

00:00:44.208 --> 00:00:47.208
Our manager's special today
is a nice chiffon cake.

00:00:47.208 --> 00:00:49.542
Ooh! We'll take two.

00:00:49.542 --> 00:00:51.250
Thank you very much.

00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:54.333
Our leader really <i>is </i>a man among men.

00:00:54.333 --> 00:00:56.042
I could kill him.

00:00:56.042 --> 00:00:59.083
You're sure making that
one cup of tea last a while.

00:00:59.083 --> 00:01:02.958
And why not? We <i>are </i>keeping
your job secret, you know.

00:01:02.958 --> 00:01:05.875
I get it. A shakedown, eh?

00:01:05.875 --> 00:01:08.167
If you'll take a second steep,
this round's on me.

00:01:08.167 --> 00:01:10.667
What a man!

00:01:10.667 --> 00:01:12.958
Carrying all that at once?

00:01:12.958 --> 00:01:14.292
What a man!

00:01:14.292 --> 00:01:17.792
Don't tell me
your mom's feeling poorly again?

00:01:17.792 --> 00:01:19.250
Yes, well...

00:01:19.250 --> 00:01:23.625
It's just me and Mom,
so I have to help out with the finances.

00:01:23.625 --> 00:01:25.042
What a man!

00:01:25.042 --> 00:01:28.125
Him being poor is his only negative.

00:01:28.125 --> 00:01:30.667
And he even turns <i>that</i>
into a cool-guy advantage!

00:01:30.667 --> 00:01:32.875
He wears his bargain-basement
clothes so neat and clean,

00:01:32.875 --> 00:01:34.792
they don't look cheap at all.

00:01:34.792 --> 00:01:34.875
What a man!

00:01:34.875 --> 00:01:34.917
What a man!

00:01:34.917 --> 00:01:36.250
"What a man!"
What a man!

00:01:36.250 --> 00:01:39.833
He let me eat some of the goldfish
he caught at the summer festival.

00:01:39.833 --> 00:01:42.292
And boy, can he cook a good goldfish!

00:01:42.292 --> 00:01:42.375
What a man!

00:01:42.375 --> 00:01:43.500
"What a man!"
What a man!

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:46.583
And after he used the bathroom?

00:01:46.583 --> 00:01:48.708
The toilet paper was folded into a triangle!

00:01:48.708 --> 00:01:48.792
What a man!

00:01:48.792 --> 00:01:49.958
"What a man!"
What a man!

00:01:50.583 --> 00:01:52.667
Hey, I fold toilet paper, too!

00:01:52.667 --> 00:01:53.792
Into a triangle!

00:01:53.792 --> 00:01:55.333
"Disgusting!"
Disgusting!

00:01:55.333 --> 00:01:58.208
Just look at him. Perfect biddy bait!

00:01:58.208 --> 00:01:59.417
"What a man!"
What a man!

00:01:59.417 --> 00:02:00.958
--Oh, Nagisa!
--Uh, middle-aged women in my neighborhood dote on me, too.

00:02:00.958 --> 00:02:02.833
--Like a widdle animal!
--Uh, middle-aged women in my neighborhood dote on me, too.

00:02:02.833 --> 00:02:02.875
Shape up!

00:02:02.875 --> 00:02:04.208
"Shape up!"
Shape up!

00:02:04.208 --> 00:02:07.375
He's still getting love letters
from girls on the main campus.

00:02:07.375 --> 00:02:07.417
What a man!

00:02:07.417 --> 00:02:08.875
"What a man!"
What a man!

00:02:08.875 --> 00:02:10.375
--Well... so am I.

00:02:10.375 --> 00:02:11.375
--For you, miss!
--Well... so am I.

00:02:11.375 --> 00:02:12.958
"Forbidden love..."
Forbidden love!

00:02:12.958 --> 00:02:18.792
Some things only suit
cool guys like Isogai... or me.

00:02:18.792 --> 00:02:20.375
What a m--

00:02:20.375 --> 00:02:21.958
What are you doing here?!

00:02:21.958 --> 00:02:25.083
The honey toast here is divine!

00:02:25.083 --> 00:02:29.292
It's why I turn a blind eye
to Isogai's part-time job.

00:02:30.458 --> 00:02:33.250
You don't seem to be too upset about Isogai

00:02:33.250 --> 00:02:35.292
being such a man among men.

00:02:35.292 --> 00:02:37.083
Huh? No.

00:02:37.083 --> 00:02:38.792
Why is that?

00:02:38.792 --> 00:02:41.125
Why?

00:02:41.125 --> 00:02:44.000
Well, because he's a good guy, that's all.

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:45.042
Uh-huh!

00:02:45.042 --> 00:02:47.167
Do we need another reason?

00:02:47.917 --> 00:02:50.042
Welcome!

00:02:50.042 --> 00:02:52.583
Oh...? Oh, dear!

00:02:52.583 --> 00:02:56.125
Our intel was right.
There <i>is </i>a student working here!

00:02:56.125 --> 00:02:58.458
Isogai, you naughty boy!

00:02:58.458 --> 00:03:01.500
This is your second
major violation of the school rules.

00:03:01.500 --> 00:03:04.792
I expected better, Isogai.

00:03:04.792 --> 00:03:07.583
Asano! This couldn't be worse.

00:03:21.458 --> 00:03:24.125
<i>You're all I think about</i>

00:03:24.125 --> 00:03:26.958
<i>Starting not to see anything else</i>

00:03:26.958 --> 00:03:32.375
<i>I'll win your heart for sure--I swear</i>

00:03:32.375 --> 00:03:35.042
<i>Me, not cool? Oh, that old tale</i>

00:03:35.042 --> 00:03:37.750
<i>I've spared no effort since then</i>

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:41.542
<i>Should be over my problems by now</i>

00:03:41.542 --> 00:03:45.542
<i>I'm brimming with confidence: I can do it</i>

00:03:45.542 --> 00:03:48.500
<i>And just when I get warmed up</i>

00:03:48.500 --> 00:03:53.708
<i>Yeah, I get knocked down like this every time</i>

00:03:53.708 --> 00:03:59.333
<i>Your scathing, serious voice cuts me</i>

00:03:59.333 --> 00:04:04.750
<i>Thousands, tens of thousands</i>
<i>of times I've given form to my feelings</i>

00:04:04.750 --> 00:04:10.250
<i>Driven them in,</i>
<i>thrown them in--but all you do is run</i>

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:12.875
<i>Question, question: what</i>

00:04:12.875 --> 00:04:15.542
<i>Question, question: on earth</i>

00:04:15.542 --> 00:04:18.333
<i>Question, question: did I</i>

00:04:18.333 --> 00:04:20.917
<i>Ever know about you anyway?</i>

00:04:20.917 --> 00:04:23.625
<i>Question, question: why</i>

00:04:23.625 --> 00:04:26.333
<i>Question, question: is it</i>

00:04:26.333 --> 00:04:29.167
<i>Question, question: you are</i>

00:04:29.167 --> 00:04:34.125
<i>So close and yet so far away?</i>

00:04:37.958 --> 00:04:42.000
"Fifth Period: Leader Time"
"by Yuma Isogai"

00:04:43.042 --> 00:04:45.417
The last time we found out about your job,

00:04:45.417 --> 00:04:48.583
you went down to the E Class.

00:04:48.583 --> 00:04:51.667
It seems you've done
no soul-searching since then.

00:04:51.667 --> 00:04:55.333
Can't you keep this quiet, Asano?

00:04:55.333 --> 00:04:59.000
Just working this month
will net me all the money I need.

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:03.875
Well, I <i>would </i>like to
give you a chance, if I can.

00:05:04.625 --> 00:05:08.125
When Asano's up to no good,

00:05:08.125 --> 00:05:10.792
he's the spitting image of the principal.

00:05:10.792 --> 00:05:14.458
All right--on one condition.

00:05:14.458 --> 00:05:19.125
Show me your fighting spirit
and we'll pretend this never happened.

00:05:19.125 --> 00:05:20.500
My fighting spirit?

00:05:20.500 --> 00:05:23.000
Per school tradition,

00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:28.000
those who possess a fighting spirit
out in society are revered above all else.

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:32.208
A fighting spirit that garners
enough respect to nullify a conduct violation.

00:05:32.208 --> 00:05:34.417
And to show that spirit...

00:05:34.417 --> 00:05:36.958
Pole-toppling at the sports festival?

00:05:36.958 --> 00:05:41.208
Yep. If we beat the A Class,
they'll let Isogai slide.

00:05:43.292 --> 00:05:48.000
Bah. Obviously they're lookin' to embarrass us.

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:52.250
So what do we do? If we say no,
Isogai'll be penalized again.

00:05:52.250 --> 00:05:55.792
Screw this up and he might even be expelled.

00:05:55.792 --> 00:05:59.375
No... you don't have to.

00:05:59.375 --> 00:06:03.833
You never know what Asano has up his sleeve.

00:06:03.833 --> 00:06:07.542
And besides, I made this bed--
I'll take responsibility and lie in it.

00:06:07.542 --> 00:06:09.208
Expel me for all I care!

00:06:09.208 --> 00:06:12.458
I can still pull off
an assassination off school grounds!

00:06:12.458 --> 00:06:15.042
Wh-What a...

00:06:15.042 --> 00:06:16.833
What a <i>horrible </i>idea!

00:06:16.833 --> 00:06:17.750
Huh?!

00:06:17.750 --> 00:06:20.042
Quit acting so self-satisfied,
you cowlicked poor!

00:06:20.042 --> 00:06:21.667
"Cowlicked poor"?!

00:06:21.667 --> 00:06:24.583
Don't overthink this, Isogai.

00:06:24.583 --> 00:06:28.667
We just have to beat those nerds
at pole-toppling, right?

00:06:28.667 --> 00:06:29.917
We've got this in the bag!

00:06:29.917 --> 00:06:34.042
We sure do. We're practically lucky
you got caught working!

00:06:34.042 --> 00:06:38.125
This is our chance to
pay 'em back for all their daily spite!

00:06:38.125 --> 00:06:40.750
Topple 'em, hell--we'll <i>destroy </i>'em!

00:06:40.750 --> 00:06:42.375
Right, Big Man?

00:06:42.375 --> 00:06:44.125
You guys...

00:06:44.750 --> 00:06:45.958
Okay, let's do it!

00:06:45.958 --> 00:06:47.583
Yeah!

00:06:47.583 --> 00:06:50.125
This is how it usually goes:

00:06:50.125 --> 00:06:53.917
putting class harmony first,
above his own needs.

00:06:53.917 --> 00:06:56.875
It all amounts to personal magnetism,

00:06:56.875 --> 00:06:59.708
the most essential attribute of a leader.

00:06:59.708 --> 00:07:04.333
Now, perhaps a fellow
man among men could lend a hand!

00:07:05.417 --> 00:07:07.167
Pole-toppling, eh?

00:07:07.167 --> 00:07:09.958
We did that plenty of times
in the Defense Academy.

00:07:09.958 --> 00:07:12.833
That's no assassination--it's war.

00:07:12.833 --> 00:07:16.333
The difference in team size
can be a huge handicap.

00:07:16.333 --> 00:07:22.167
They're well-trained, but can they
best a team nearly twice as big?

00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:30.000
"Entrance"

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:32.750
"Water Gods" "Mighty Warriors" "Sure Victory"

00:07:34.375 --> 00:07:36.667
Woo! Awesome, Kimura!

00:07:36.667 --> 00:07:36.875
Smile even bigger now! That's it, Justice!

00:07:36.875 --> 00:07:39.750
"Koro Sensei's Weak Point #27: Acts like a proud parent"
Smile even bigger now! That's it, Justice!

00:07:46.125 --> 00:07:48.708
Bread is for drinking.

00:07:48.708 --> 00:07:50.208
Too cool!

00:07:50.208 --> 00:07:54.875
Yes--assassination has improved
your physical fitness, balance,

00:07:54.875 --> 00:07:56.792
kinetic vision, and sense of distance.

00:07:56.792 --> 00:07:58.333
--That's harassment!
--This extraordinary competition is sure to show them off.

00:07:58.333 --> 00:07:59.500
--Huh?
--This extraordinary competition is sure to show them off.

00:07:59.500 --> 00:08:02.125
Look how fast that runt
is crawling through the net!

00:08:02.125 --> 00:08:04.833
Her body's got no resistance!

00:08:04.833 --> 00:08:07.833
Each student's individuality
will be their weapon.

00:08:07.833 --> 00:08:14.125
It's up to you how best to use
that in pole-toppling, Isogai.

00:08:14.125 --> 00:08:16.000
What is it?

00:08:16.000 --> 00:08:18.625
Koro Sensei, no matter what anyone says,

00:08:18.625 --> 00:08:20.583
Asano is one amazing guy.

00:08:20.583 --> 00:08:20.958
"Pole-Toppling Strategy Book"
Asano is one amazing guy.

00:08:20.958 --> 00:08:23.583
"Pole-Toppling Strategy Book"
I'm definitely no match for him.

00:08:26.542 --> 00:08:30.167
It's true that no matter how talented you are,

00:08:30.167 --> 00:08:33.500
once you're out in the world,
there will always be someone better.

00:08:33.500 --> 00:08:35.208
Like he is.

00:08:35.208 --> 00:08:39.708
What now?
If everyone gets hurt because of me...

00:08:39.708 --> 00:08:41.625
The thing is...

00:08:41.625 --> 00:08:45.083
Out in the world,
one person has only so much power.

00:08:45.083 --> 00:08:47.083
Yeah!

00:08:47.083 --> 00:08:50.417
The power to command allies into battle:

00:08:50.417 --> 00:08:53.833
That's where you've got Asano beat.

00:08:53.833 --> 00:08:58.875
If you find yourself in a pinch,
everyone will fight alongside you.

00:08:58.875 --> 00:09:01.583
That's your personal magnetism.

00:09:01.583 --> 00:09:07.667
And as for me, I'm glad I got to be
your teacher instead of Asano's.

00:09:10.083 --> 00:09:11.792
All right, guys!

00:09:11.792 --> 00:09:14.167
Let's go into this guns blazing--like always!

00:09:14.167 --> 00:09:15.833
Yeah!

00:09:15.833 --> 00:09:15.958
"Broadcast Booth"
Yeah!

00:09:15.958 --> 00:09:17.875
"Broadcast Booth"
Now for an exhibition match!

00:09:17.875 --> 00:09:20.333
"Broadcast Booth"
Seems the E Class has challenged the A Class to a battle!

00:09:20.333 --> 00:09:22.125
Seems the E Class has challenged the A Class to a battle!

00:09:22.125 --> 00:09:25.583
Okay, Kunugigaoka's elite--give 'em hell!

00:09:26.125 --> 00:09:27.167
Foreigners?

00:09:27.167 --> 00:09:29.167
That's gotta be against the rules!

00:09:29.167 --> 00:09:32.958
And in the spirit of cultural exchange,
this exhibition match

00:09:32.958 --> 00:09:35.417
will include all our exchange students!

00:09:35.417 --> 00:09:38.208
That Asano's being way too careful.

00:09:38.208 --> 00:09:40.708
Is that how badly he wants to win?

00:09:42.708 --> 00:09:44.458
This is gonna be good.

00:09:44.458 --> 00:09:48.167
What will the E Class do now?

00:09:49.917 --> 00:09:53.083
If the E Class wants to
win with so few members,

00:09:53.083 --> 00:09:55.833
they'll have to abandon defense and attack--

00:09:55.833 --> 00:09:59.542
only to get swallowed up by our ironclad defense and be crushed.

00:09:59.542 --> 00:10:01.625
"Asano" "Initial A-Class Formation: Defend & Destroy"
only to get swallowed up by our ironclad defense and be crushed.

00:10:02.167 --> 00:10:05.500
Hey--does the End Class even <i>want </i>to win?

00:10:05.500 --> 00:10:07.917
No one's on offense!

00:10:07.917 --> 00:10:08.167
What's with the E Class? They're going all-in on defense!

00:10:08.167 --> 00:10:11.125
"Initial E-Class Formation: Absolute Defense Form"
What's with the E Class? They're going all-in on defense!

00:10:11.125 --> 00:10:11.833
What's with the E Class? They're going all-in on defense!

00:10:11.833 --> 00:10:14.792
Might they be cowed by the skill gap?

00:10:14.792 --> 00:10:18.042
Let the battle begin!

00:10:18.042 --> 00:10:19.875
Bring it on, Asano!

00:10:19.875 --> 00:10:23.625
Trying to lure us out, eh?
You underestimate us.

00:10:23.625 --> 00:10:25.625
Offense team, Plan F!

00:10:25.625 --> 00:10:27.125
Roger!

00:10:28.667 --> 00:10:32.250
We're not trying to bring down the pole.

00:10:32.250 --> 00:10:34.333
No, we mean to crush you--once and for all.

00:10:34.333 --> 00:10:35.708
"E-Class Main Unit"
No, we mean to crush you--once and for all.

00:10:35.708 --> 00:10:35.917
No, we mean to crush you--once and for all.

00:10:35.917 --> 00:10:38.167
Whoa! Here they come!

00:10:40.500 --> 00:10:41.375
Dammit!

00:10:41.375 --> 00:10:44.083
We're not just gonna roll over and take this!

00:10:48.083 --> 00:10:49.542
"Fight to the Finish" "Bravery!"

00:10:49.542 --> 00:10:51.208
"Fight to the Finish" "Bravery!"
Two down!

00:10:51.208 --> 00:10:53.917
They've been flung out to the stands!

00:10:54.667 --> 00:10:56.625
Th-This isn't good, Koro Sensei!

00:10:56.625 --> 00:11:01.333
A tight defense doesn't matter
if they just get picked off one by one!

00:11:01.333 --> 00:11:04.875
Why don't you fight instead of
defending like a bunch of turtles?

00:11:04.875 --> 00:11:07.542
Hmph. But you don't even
understand me, do you.

00:11:07.542 --> 00:11:09.292
It's all right, man.

00:11:09.292 --> 00:11:12.292
Why don't you attack instead of chatting away?

00:11:12.292 --> 00:11:15.000
Hmph. Bring it on!

00:11:16.542 --> 00:11:17.708
Okay, guys--now!

00:11:17.708 --> 00:11:19.750
Operation: Tentacles!

00:11:22.750 --> 00:11:24.583
"E-Class Formation: Tentacle Tangle"

00:11:24.583 --> 00:11:26.125
Pin 'em down!

00:11:26.917 --> 00:11:30.875
The E Class comes together
with the weight of the pole!

00:11:30.875 --> 00:11:33.625
Now this is intense! They're playing dirty!

00:11:33.625 --> 00:11:37.083
Ain't no rule against
usin' the pole as a weapon!

00:11:37.083 --> 00:11:38.875
Get off of me!

00:11:38.875 --> 00:11:40.292
You're not goin' anywhere!

00:11:40.292 --> 00:11:42.292
A splendid defense.

00:11:42.292 --> 00:11:47.125
But you've got seven men strictly on defense,
and two are out for the count.

00:11:47.125 --> 00:11:50.333
We just have even more of an advantage now.

00:11:50.333 --> 00:11:51.917
Guerilla teams on both flanks:

00:11:51.917 --> 00:11:53.708
Plan K!

00:11:56.125 --> 00:11:58.750
There's a gap right in the middle.
If we're going to attack,

00:11:58.750 --> 00:12:01.583
it has to be now,
when their forces are scattered!

00:12:01.583 --> 00:12:02.708
Come on out!

00:12:02.708 --> 00:12:05.250
Attack team! Operation: Mucus!

00:12:05.250 --> 00:12:05.708
Got it!

00:12:05.708 --> 00:12:06.917
"Total Victory"
Got it!

00:12:06.917 --> 00:12:08.292
"E-Class Main Unit" "Isogai"

00:12:08.292 --> 00:12:10.833
Got 'em.

00:12:10.833 --> 00:12:14.792
Oh! They've chased after the E Class
and are back on the defensive!

00:12:14.792 --> 00:12:18.375
An offensive fake-out?!

00:12:18.375 --> 00:12:20.417
It's like a chess problem.

00:12:20.417 --> 00:12:20.958
Even though they've made their defensive line airtight...

00:12:20.958 --> 00:12:23.583
"A Class: Plan K" "Feint -> Pincer Attack"
Even though they've made their defensive line airtight...

00:12:23.583 --> 00:12:23.750
Even though they've made their defensive line airtight...

00:12:23.750 --> 00:12:26.875
the tide of battle is turning against them.

00:12:29.083 --> 00:12:33.083
"Assassination Classroom, Second Season"
"by Karma Akabane"

00:12:35.625 --> 00:12:37.500
What should we do?

00:12:37.500 --> 00:12:41.583
The Defense Ministry
would rather no one get injured.

00:12:42.958 --> 00:12:47.625
It's all right. I gave him some tips
in our social studies work.

00:12:48.333 --> 00:12:50.958
As a good example of
defeating a group twice your size,

00:12:50.958 --> 00:12:54.458
I'm rather fond of Hannibal of Carthage.

00:12:54.458 --> 00:12:57.792
Oh--the scourge of ancient Rome.

00:12:57.792 --> 00:12:59.792
He sent his troops where there were no roads,

00:12:59.792 --> 00:13:03.708
popping up in places
where the foe was unprepared.

00:13:03.708 --> 00:13:07.792
He thought up defenses
and used secret weapons.

00:13:07.792 --> 00:13:11.083
Put a touch of the unconventional
in all of your strategies.

00:13:11.083 --> 00:13:15.417
They can carry out whatever
clever schemes you put together.

00:13:18.250 --> 00:13:19.667
"Isogai"

00:13:19.667 --> 00:13:20.250
"Isogai"
Ooh! Those E Class losers are totally surrounded!

00:13:20.250 --> 00:13:23.667
"Fight to the Finish"
Ooh! Those E Class losers are totally surrounded!

00:13:23.667 --> 00:13:24.375
"Fight to the Finish"
It's beatin' time!

00:13:24.375 --> 00:13:26.167
"Isogai"
It's beatin' time!

00:13:26.167 --> 00:13:28.375
"Isogai"
H-Hey, wait! Ack!

00:13:28.375 --> 00:13:28.417
"Fight to the Finish"
H-Hey, wait! Ack!

00:13:28.417 --> 00:13:32.000
"Fight to the Finish"
Why are they all headed this way?!

00:13:32.000 --> 00:13:33.125
"Fight to the Finish"

00:13:34.125 --> 00:13:34.375
"E-Class Formation: Mucus Hell"

00:13:34.375 --> 00:13:37.458
"E-Class Formation: Mucus Hell"
The E Class has begun fleeing to the stands!

00:13:37.458 --> 00:13:38.625
"E-Class Formation: Mucus Hell"
The whole place is in a panic!

00:13:38.625 --> 00:13:39.625
The whole place is in a panic!

00:13:39.625 --> 00:13:43.292
There are no rules about boundaries. Come on.

00:13:43.292 --> 00:13:45.833
The whole school is a battlefield.

00:13:45.833 --> 00:13:49.875
What are you doing? Quick, stop them!

00:13:49.875 --> 00:13:52.458
The most dangerous part of pole-toppling

00:13:52.458 --> 00:13:57.125
is that even with a handful of people,
you can make it to the top.

00:13:57.125 --> 00:13:59.042
Who can pull that off?

00:13:59.042 --> 00:14:00.417
Akabane!

00:14:00.417 --> 00:14:01.375
Kimura!

00:14:01.375 --> 00:14:04.208
And Isogai! Keep an eye
on those three in particular!

00:14:04.208 --> 00:14:08.167
Yuma Isogai... If the E Class loses this,

00:14:08.167 --> 00:14:08.417
"Notice of Expulsion"
Yuma Isogai... If the E Class loses this,

00:14:08.417 --> 00:14:12.292
"Notice of Expulsion"
I'll report your infraction and you'll be out in the cold.

00:14:12.292 --> 00:14:15.625
"Notice of Expulsion"
Don't like it? Then you'll have to command everyone to attack.

00:14:15.625 --> 00:14:16.417
Don't like it? Then you'll have to command everyone to attack.

00:14:16.417 --> 00:14:21.042
Either you fall alone
or you drag them all down with you:

00:14:21.042 --> 00:14:24.792
the choice is yours, E Class leader.

00:14:24.792 --> 00:14:28.042
Isogai! It's about that time!

00:14:28.042 --> 00:14:31.583
Yep! So far, it's all according to plan!

00:14:37.917 --> 00:14:42.458
What?! Where did those two
E Class goons come from?

00:14:42.458 --> 00:14:44.833
We practiced taking blows
till we were blue in the face.

00:14:44.833 --> 00:14:48.042
The only hard part was
acting out that flight to the stands!

00:14:48.042 --> 00:14:51.292
Are these the ones thrown to
the stands at the beginning?!

00:14:51.292 --> 00:14:53.417
We're done running! Okay, team: Sonic!

00:14:53.417 --> 00:14:54.875
"Fight to the Finish"
We're done running! Okay, team: Sonic!

00:14:54.875 --> 00:14:56.917
"Fight to the Finish"
All right!

00:14:57.708 --> 00:14:59.292
I get it...

00:14:59.292 --> 00:14:59.708
While everyone was focused on the scuffle,

00:14:59.708 --> 00:15:02.125
"A-Class Main Unit" "E-Class Main Unit"
While everyone was focused on the scuffle,

00:15:02.125 --> 00:15:05.250
"A-Class Main Unit" "E-Class Main Unit"
the two who faked injuries to leave the field formed another unit

00:15:05.250 --> 00:15:07.208
"A-Class Main Unit" "E-Class Main Unit"
and sneaked in from outside!

00:15:07.208 --> 00:15:11.417
"A-Class Main Unit" "E-Class Main Unit"
Then they used <i>that </i>disturbance to rush the A Class's main unit!

00:15:11.417 --> 00:15:13.042
So <i>that's </i>their game!

00:15:13.042 --> 00:15:14.375
<i>That's </i>our game!

00:15:14.375 --> 00:15:14.833
"E-Class Formation: Sonic Flight"

00:15:14.833 --> 00:15:16.375
"E-Class Formation: Sonic Flight"
Ack! They got right up in our faces!

00:15:16.375 --> 00:15:18.000
Ack! They got right up in our faces!

00:15:18.000 --> 00:15:19.792
Take that, Asano!

00:15:19.792 --> 00:15:24.042
There might be fewer of us,
but as long as we can get up here...

00:15:30.833 --> 00:15:33.375
Does he know martial arts, too?!

00:15:34.042 --> 00:15:38.333
You and I are standing on the same stage.

00:15:39.417 --> 00:15:43.958
Surely you're prepared to get kicked off.

00:15:43.958 --> 00:15:48.208
That last-boss vibe--
that's the principal's son for you!

00:15:49.708 --> 00:15:51.792
Uh-oh--they're closing in.

00:15:51.792 --> 00:15:55.500
At this rate, they'll be surrounded
and beaten to a pulp!

00:15:55.500 --> 00:16:00.125
Asano is a strong leader who can
singlehandedly decide the tide of battle.

00:16:00.125 --> 00:16:03.792
As long as they follow his command,
the A Class can't lose.

00:16:05.083 --> 00:16:08.500
Isogai, you likely can't be that kind of leader.

00:16:08.500 --> 00:16:10.250
And that's because...

00:16:10.250 --> 00:16:13.500
you don't have to make
all the decisions yourself!

00:16:15.125 --> 00:16:16.542
--What?!
--No! Not <i>more </i>E-Class reinforcements!

00:16:16.542 --> 00:16:18.917
--No! Not <i>more </i>E-Class reinforcements!

00:16:18.917 --> 00:16:21.958
Wait a second! Isn't that their defensive unit?

00:16:21.958 --> 00:16:23.375
Which means...

00:16:23.375 --> 00:16:25.375
The E Class only has two men on defense?!

00:16:25.375 --> 00:16:27.417
How are they keeping them down?!

00:16:27.417 --> 00:16:29.083
Leverage.

00:16:29.083 --> 00:16:29.208
"Fight to the Finish"
Leverage.

00:16:29.208 --> 00:16:30.083
"Fight to the Finish"
Lev--?

00:16:30.083 --> 00:16:32.500
"Fight to the Finish"
Leverage, is it?

00:16:32.500 --> 00:16:35.875
They seem perfectly happy with that answer.

00:16:35.875 --> 00:16:38.000
It's a stall, of course.

00:16:38.000 --> 00:16:41.125
We two can't really hold them all back.

00:16:41.125 --> 00:16:45.708
But you guys can't do anything
without orders, can you?

00:16:45.708 --> 00:16:49.208
Maybe he still has an ace up his sleeve.

00:16:49.208 --> 00:16:54.292
I guess it's better to wait for his orders
before you make any moves.

00:16:54.292 --> 00:16:55.833
Damn four-eyes!

00:16:55.833 --> 00:16:58.750
Asano! Your orders!

00:16:58.750 --> 00:17:01.000
I can't give any orders!

00:17:01.000 --> 00:17:03.667
Now the A Class has assumed
a defensive posture, too!

00:17:03.667 --> 00:17:07.375
If they can hold out here,
the E Class will be out of options!

00:17:07.375 --> 00:17:10.292
Now! Come on, Itona!

00:17:10.292 --> 00:17:11.708
Yep.

00:17:12.917 --> 00:17:16.333
A secret weapon is meant
to be saved for the last minute.

00:17:22.875 --> 00:17:24.542
We're losing?

00:17:34.625 --> 00:17:35.542
"Fight to the Finish"

00:17:35.542 --> 00:17:38.375
"Fight to the Finish"
Uh... er... the A Class...

00:17:38.375 --> 00:17:39.958
The E Class...

00:17:39.958 --> 00:17:42.042
wins!

00:17:43.167 --> 00:17:47.125
How cool is that? My kids are
the coolest! Look this way, please!

00:17:47.125 --> 00:17:49.542
You did it, Isogai!

00:17:50.042 --> 00:17:53.500
Anyone can see that,
by some miracle, the E Team won a battle

00:17:53.500 --> 00:17:56.458
that was clearly not in their favor.

00:17:56.458 --> 00:18:00.375
In short, you got owned.

00:18:00.375 --> 00:18:03.667
Isogai used your strategy against you

00:18:03.667 --> 00:18:07.292
and ensured victory
with a hidden secret weapon.

00:18:07.292 --> 00:18:10.542
When it came to the info war,
you'd already lost.

00:18:10.542 --> 00:18:13.292
You're not fit to be a leader.

00:18:13.292 --> 00:18:17.125
Chief Director, your son is extremely capable.

00:18:17.125 --> 00:18:17.917
Stop it, Kevin!

00:18:17.917 --> 00:18:20.000
As a father, you should tell him

00:18:20.000 --> 00:18:23.458
that there's a lot he can learn from losing.

00:18:23.458 --> 00:18:29.167
I see... Your little opinion
is quite moving, Kevin.

00:18:29.167 --> 00:18:31.542
Could you help me learn as well?

00:18:31.542 --> 00:18:33.667
If I were to lose,

00:18:33.667 --> 00:18:37.375
I might be able to learn from that loss.

00:18:37.375 --> 00:18:42.042
All four at once... please.

00:18:46.333 --> 00:18:48.458
Isogai!

00:18:48.458 --> 00:18:50.000
You were so awesome!

00:18:50.000 --> 00:18:51.542
Hey, thanks!

00:18:51.542 --> 00:18:53.042
Just don't try that at home.

00:18:53.042 --> 00:18:55.750
--Squee!
--Damn that man-among-men!

00:18:55.750 --> 00:18:59.042
It's like the whole mood's
changed around here.

00:18:59.042 --> 00:19:01.833
Especially with how the
lower grades see the E Class now.

00:19:01.833 --> 00:19:06.958
Well, sure, with our little team's huge upset!

00:19:06.958 --> 00:19:08.375
You know...

00:19:08.375 --> 00:19:11.792
we might even be more amazing
than Asano and his gang!

00:19:17.208 --> 00:19:22.667
Sorry... I'm sorry... I apologize...

00:19:22.667 --> 00:19:26.708
I took down a karate black belt

00:19:26.708 --> 00:19:29.458
on my third day of karate lessons.

00:19:29.458 --> 00:19:34.292
The first day, this thirty-something
guy beat me but good.

00:19:34.292 --> 00:19:39.250
I fell over, vomiting.
I had never tasted such defeat.

00:19:39.250 --> 00:19:43.167
Now, what do you think I did on day two?

00:19:43.167 --> 00:19:48.958
I watched, burning with the flames
of extraordinary humiliation.

00:19:48.958 --> 00:19:51.167
If I lost my next match, too...

00:19:51.167 --> 00:19:56.958
I'd probably lose my grip on
my personality and die of madness.

00:19:58.167 --> 00:20:03.875
And on day three... I took down
my teacher without him landing a blow.

00:20:03.875 --> 00:20:07.083
<i>That's </i>learning from defeat.

00:20:08.042 --> 00:20:10.542
Say, Asano...

00:20:10.542 --> 00:20:18.250
If you lost, then why isn't
the frustration eating you alive?

00:20:18.250 --> 00:20:20.333
You monster!

00:20:24.375 --> 00:20:26.500
Hey, check it out...

00:20:26.500 --> 00:20:29.417
Oh--it's Asano.

00:20:29.417 --> 00:20:31.542
Hey, Asano!

00:20:31.542 --> 00:20:36.500
You meant it, right?
About keeping that secret?

00:20:36.500 --> 00:20:39.208
I never lie.

00:20:39.208 --> 00:20:43.250
I don't resort to
underhanded tactics, unlike you.

00:20:43.250 --> 00:20:49.125
But next time will be different.
I'll chase you all into oblivion.

00:20:49.125 --> 00:20:51.375
Heh. Sore loser.

00:20:51.375 --> 00:20:55.708
Hey, big words from
a big loser fall on deaf ears!

00:20:55.708 --> 00:21:00.667
Don't sweat it.
He can't understand your struggle.

00:21:00.667 --> 00:21:06.458
No, it's not like I've gone through
any more than he has.

00:21:06.458 --> 00:21:08.958
Today, with all you helping me out,

00:21:08.958 --> 00:21:12.375
I was actually glad to be poor.

00:21:12.375 --> 00:21:15.500
--Shake it off, Asano. Let's go tie this up with a fancy dinner.
--He may not be as showy as Asano,

00:21:15.500 --> 00:21:18.875
--Shake it off, Asano. Let's go tie this up with a fancy dinner.
--but Isogai's not in front or on top:

00:21:18.875 --> 00:21:21.125
he's beside you before you know it.

00:21:21.125 --> 00:21:23.625
Whoa! Leftovers from
the bread-eating contest!

00:21:23.625 --> 00:21:26.333
--The president of Class 3-E
--Think I could have these? Huh?

00:21:26.333 --> 00:21:28.000
--is a cool and manly leader of an assassin.
--Think I could have these? Huh?

00:21:28.000 --> 00:21:30.500
--is a cool and manly leader of an assassin.
--I know! I'll make goldfish buns!

00:21:42.583 --> 00:21:48.083
<i>The moon that swims in the night sky</i>

00:21:48.083 --> 00:21:53.458
<i>If you stretch out your hand, you can reach it</i>

00:21:53.458 --> 00:21:59.125
<i>I went to touch it: it was warm</i>

00:21:59.125 --> 00:22:04.292
<i>And slowly drew me in</i>

00:22:04.292 --> 00:22:15.667
<i>The multiplying footsteps,</i>
<i>the view from my window:</i>

00:22:15.667 --> 00:22:21.250
<i>As I drifted along, expressionless</i>

00:22:21.250 --> 00:22:25.667
<i>They spilled out of my hands</i>

00:22:25.667 --> 00:22:32.500
<i>It was rocking, swaying--I never knew</i>

00:22:32.500 --> 00:22:38.000
<i>Until I touched it with my own hands</i>

00:22:38.000 --> 00:22:43.500
<i>I'll gather up</i>
<i>and go through all of the things</i>

00:22:43.500 --> 00:23:02.144
<i>Scattered beneath the waning moon</i>
